  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GA 2024 PC 42043 //   LOT 6: Technical and Support Services to the EU Programmatic Processes in the occupied Palestinian territories</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The Global Objective of this contract is to improve the overall effectiveness of the European Union Representation (EUREP) in the phases of programmatic identification, formulation, monitoring and knowledge capture, in multiple sectors, in the occupied Palestinian territories.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The Specific Objective of the contract is to provide technical and support services to improve the EU&#xbf;s programmatic processes in the occupied Palestinian territories. This includes three streams of work which frame the Results of this TOR as articulated below:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;1.To provide technical and support services throughout the whole programme cycle (identification, design, formulation, monitoring and evaluation)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;2.To reinforce the technical capacities of stakeholders and in particular EU staff, throughout the whole programme cycle.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;3.To prepare specific products (studies, guidelines, etc.) and provide advisory services on specific queries.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The above-mentioned support should be provided through a `Facility for Operational and Programmatic support&#xbf; across multiple sectors of work where the EUREP currently is, or wishes to develop, its programmes. It should also respond to the dynamic context across the West Bank, Gaza and East Jerusalem, and enhance the EU&#xbf;s ability to adjust programming as necessary.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
